 Maritime Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/South_Australian_Maritime_Museum_building_in_South_Australia%2C_June_2026_%28028A6607%29.jpg/960px-South_Australian_Maritime_Museum_building_in_South_Australia%2C_June_2026_%28028A6607%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Clipper Ship City of Adelaide","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":-34.837456,"lo":138.508466,"d":1261},{"n":"Carrosel","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-34.837387,"lo":138.480218,"d":1380},{"n":"National Rail Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-34.846062,"lo":138.508911,"d":1437,"h":"Mo-Su,PH 10:00-16:30","w":"https://nrm.org.au/","ph":"+61 8 8341 1690","wp":"en:National Railway Museum (Port Adelaide)","ds":"The National Railway Museum, Port Adelaide, South Australia is the largest under-cover railway museum in Australia. More than 100 major exhibits, mainly from the South Australian Railways (SAR), Commonwealth Railways (CR) and their successor, Australian National (AN), are displayed at its 3.5-hectare (8.6-acre) site.","wpu":"National Railway Museum, Port Adelaide","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Ron_Fitch_Pavilion_at_National_Railway_Museum%2C_Port_Adelaide%2C_2014.jpg/960px-Ron_Fitch_Pavilion_at_National_Railway_Museum%2C_Port_Adelaide%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"South Australian Aviation Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-34.848233,"lo":138.511858,"d":1790,"h":"Mo-Su 10:00-16:00","w":"http://www.saam.org.au","ph":"+61 8 8240 1230","wp":"en:South Australian Aviation Museum","ds":"The South Australian Aviation Museum, located in Port Adelaide, South Australia, is an aviation museum which displays aircraft, aircraft engines, and rockets of relevance to South Australia, and the history of aviation and the aerospace industry in Australia.","wpu":"South Australian Aviation Museum"},{"n":"Fort Glanville","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":-34.851059,"lo":138.477552,"d":2011},{"n":"Fort Glanville Conservation Park","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-34.851787,"lo":138.478072,"d":2025,"wp":"en:Fort Glanville Conservation Park","ds":"Fort Glanville Conservation Park is a protected area located in the Australian state of South Australia located in Semaphore Park, a seaside suburb of Adelaide consisting of a functional 19th century fort listed on the South Australian Heritage Register and some adjoining land used as a caravan park. The fort was built after more than 40 years of indecision over the defence of South Australia.","wpu":"Fort Glanville Conservation Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/64_pounder_gun_firing_-_fort_glanville.jpg/960px-64_pounder_gun_firing_-_fort_glanville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Adelaide Beachfront Tourist Park","g":"sights","k":"caravan_site","la":-34.852354,"lo":138.477901,"d":2078,"wifi":1},{"n":"Port Misery","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-34.85924,"lo":138.500298,"d":2193},{"n":"Semaphore Park Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":-34.857253,"lo":138.475607,"d":2609},{"n":"West Lakes Shore Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":-34.871712,"lo":138.479442,"d":3801},{"n":"Ships Graveyard","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-34.811556,"lo":138.528738,"d":4414},{"n":"Tennyson Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":-34.888103,"lo":138.484473,"d":5434},{"n":"Dolphin Sanctuary Kayak Tours","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-34.803864,"lo":138.539206,"d":5694,"w":"https://dolphinsanctuarykayaktours.com.au/"},{"n":"Grange Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":-34.90253,"lo":138.488186,"d":6980},{"n":"Charles Sturt Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-34.903,"lo":138.498346,"d":7011,"h":"Su 10:00-04:00","w":"https://www.charlessturtmuseum.com.au/","ph":"+61 8 8356 8185"},{"n":"Henley Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":-34.921688,"lo":138.493327,"d":9084},{"n":"Craig Roberts Pharmacy",