ttps://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/TomDiverDerrickBridgeJuly08.jpg/960px-TomDiverDerrickBridgeJuly08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Semaphore Library","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.838679,"lo":138.481337,"d":1255,"ds":"The Semaphore Library is a public library in Semaphore, South Australia. It was formerly the Semaphore Institute, Semaphore Town Hall, Ozone Theatre, and Semaphore Cinema, and is heritage-listed on both the state and national registers.","wpu":"Semaphore Library","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Semaphore_Town_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Port Adelaide Uniting Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.846884,"lo":138.507611,"d":1382,"ds":"The Port Adelaide Uniting Church is located in Port Adelaide, South Australia. It is an active church, with worship and prayer each week.","wpu":"Port Adelaide Uniting Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Port_Adelaide_Uniting_Church_in_South_Australia%2C_June_2026_%28028A7151%29.jpg/960px-Port_Adelaide_Uniting_Church_in_South_Australia%2C_June_2026_%28028A7151%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Largs Pier Hotel","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.8256,"lo":138.4865,"d":1779,"ds":"Largs Pier Hotel is located on the corner of The Esplanade and Jetty Road in Largs Bay, South Australia.","wpu":"Largs Pier Hotel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Largs_Pier_Hotel_1900.jpg/960px-Largs_Pier_Hotel_1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Rosewater Uniting Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.851754,"lo":138.518998,"d":2550,"ds":"The Rosewater Uniting Church was a Uniting church located in Rosewater, South Australia. The former Methodist church was founded as a Primitive Methodist church in 1878. The foundation stone was laid by the Chairman of the District Council of Rosewater, H. C. E. Muecke on 10 August, and the opening services were held on 24 November 1878.","wpu":"Rosewater Uniting Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Rosewater_uniting_church_front_new.jpg/960px-Rosewater_uniting_church_front_new.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Royal Park, South Australia","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.872,"lo":138.508,"d":3750,"ds":"Royal Park is located in the western suburbs of Adelaide. It is home to a large Polish community, as evidenced by the establishment of St Stanislaus of Cracow Catholic Church. Other ethnic groups represented include Italian, Croatian, Bosnian, Irish, Macedonian and Greek.","wpu":"Royal Park, South Australia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Cooke_Reserve_wetland.JPG/960px-Cooke_Reserve_wetland.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pháp Hoa Temple","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-34.857144,"lo":138.533385,"d":3987,"ds":"Phap Hoa Temple (Vietnamese: Chùa Pháp Hoa, , Chữ Hán: 法葩寺), meaning Dharma Lotus Temple, is a Buddhist temple located in Pennington, South Australia. Established in 1978, it moved to its current location in December 1989. It is a member of the United Vietnamese Buddhist Congregation and the head is the Most Venerable Thich Nhu Hue, and the abbot is the Reverend Thich Vien Tri.","wpu":"Pháp Hoa Temple","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Phap_hoa_2.JPG/960px-Phap_hoa_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Adelaide ( AD-il-ayd; Kaurna: Tarndanya [ˈd̪̥aɳɖaɲa]) is the capital and most populous city of South Australia, as well as the fifth-most populous city in Australia. The name \"Adelaide\" may refer to either Greater Adelaide (including the Adelaide Hills) or the Adelaide central business district; the demonym Adelaidean is used to denote the city and the residents of Adelaide. The traditional owners of the Adelaide region are the Kaurna, with the name Tarndanya referring to the area of the city centre and surrounding Park Lands, in the Kaurna language.","wpu":"Adelaide","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Adelaide_skyline%2C_December_2022_b.jpg/960px-Adelaide_skyline%2C_December_2022_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}